3. Where the comparison vectors in tests/vectors/noise/ came from. These are
   numeric outputs, not copies of code; they are recorded so the provenance is
   not a guess.

   tests/vectors/noise/fnl/  pyfastnoiselite (a Cython binding of FastNoiseLite),
                             MIT licence per its PyPI classifier. Also an
                             optional runtime extra ("reference").
   tests/vectors/noise/fns/  pyfastnoisesimd (a binding of FastNoiseSIMD),
                             BSD-3-Clause per its PyPI metadata. Its last
                             release is 2021-03-31 and it is no longer a
                             dependency; it was used once, on Python 3.9, to
                             capture these files.
   domain warp vectors       generated by the C++ harness in tools/noise_oracle
                             over the vendored FastNoiseLite.h.
